[[File:The Vessel (Beta 52.0).png|thumb|Beta 52.0]]
The Vessel was added in '''Beta 51.0, '''as the 8th [[:Category:Determination (Rarity)|Determination]] monster. It was a 12G 6/6 monster that added 4 exact copies of an ally monster to your deck and 1 to your hand. (It couldn't target other Vessels.) This made it function much like [[Alphys|Royal Integrity]], thus an old [[Cloning]], only on a much grander scale. '''Beta 52.0''' gave it -2G, but also made it add 2 copies to your deck instead of 4 (while still adding 1 to your hand).
[[File:The Vessel (Beta 56.0).png|thumb|Beta 56.0]]
'''Beta 56.0''' made it no longer able to copy any other DT monster. After its effect, it will also transform itself into the True Vessel, which is the same 6/6 but without any effects, preventing repeated use. As a trade off, True Vessel is a mere 2G, so bouncing it will not have a big impact. '''Beta 57.1''' made True Vessel keep the buffs The Vessel obtained beforehand.

